This file gathers and re-exports the development of Exercise 8.12(b) (Scott 1981,
PRG-19, Lecture VIII), the computable presentation of the neighbourhood system V. It
includes iterated division and remainder by a power of two and their correctness; the
bit test, its bound, and its characterization; the low-bit conjunction and the iterative
bitwise conjunction, with the step, the one-step recursion, and the iteration invariant;
upsampling of a level mask by the one-step and joint iterations, together with the
level-set identities; the bounded nonemptiness test; canonicalization of a
level-and-mask code, its idempotence, and the nonemptiness of the result; the
enumeration, membership, surjectivity, and the master index; the raw and canonical
intersection codes and Scott's two relations; and the assembled computable presentation.
